# Email and 6-digit codes (first-party)

- We implement mail + verification in Icerde (`services/api` + UI). **No AgentMail, no inbox SaaS MCP, no SMS.**
- Transport is SMTP (`SMTP_*`) or Resend HTTP (`RESEND_API_KEY`) from **our** Go process. Missing both in dev → in-app `tempMailboxes` + `emailSent: false` (never a fake “sent”). Production: `ICERDE_MAIL_REQUIRE=1`.
- Store only `codeHash` (pepper + SHA-256), ~10 min TTL, max 5 attempts, one active code per purpose (new code invalidates old).
- Purposes: `new_device`, `login_challenge`, `email_verify`, `suspicious_login`. Exhaustive switch with `never` / Go equivalent.
- Link token and 6-digit UI both resolve the same record.
- Temp mailbox is our Mongo collection + Security UI, not a third-party inbox.
- Read [docs/email-verification.md](docs/email-verification.md) and [docs/security.md](docs/security.md).
